}.items():\n    code = P.verify_cycle(R.RICH_RUNTIME_ID, x[\"input\"], hashes, x[\"nodes\"], wire)\n    print(\"experimental-control\", name, code)\nprint(\"FAIL CYCLE-JSON: malformed wire encodings reached Book I replay\" if violations else \"ok CYCLE-JSON\")\nraise SystemExit(1 if violations else 0)\n","review":"roadmap G1 verdict by codex","scope":"The Book I counterexample proves replay of malformed wire encodings, not acceptance of a Book I cycle. An additional positive control uses the explicitly experimental M M rich profile: malformed encodings return CYCLE_PROVEN there too. That control is not offered as a cycle in the standard Book I profile.","severity":"P2","sources":["https://github.com/s0fractal/sigma-glyph/releases/tag/v1.0.0","https://github.com/s0fractal/sigma-glyph/actions/runs/41339906440","https://pypi.org/pypi/sigma-glyph/1.0.0/json"],"statement":"The released sigma-resume provider does not enforce the normative canonical cycle-witness wire encoding and malformed-witness refusal before replay.","target":"ca9441958a950d4f26e2f05ac97e6620ae16b28947e6dcc24025a88502972d19","verdict":"challenge","where":["spec/sigma-resume.md:104","spec/sigma-resume.md:114","impl/sigma_provider.py:246","impl/sigma_provider.py:249","impl/sigma_resume.py:566","tests/resume_claims_test.py:196"]}